--
sv-benchmarks pthread-race-challenges/thread-join-counter-outer-race-4 (MIT),
with the options of the SV-COMP wrapper. The race is on `data`: the read in
main (line 715, `return data`) and the write in a created thread (line 692).
The model leaves the phase symbols of other accesses free, and those of
`threads_alive` held as well; the witness then paired the read of `data` with
the write of `threads_alive` on line 695, which is no race. The two accesses
kept in the trace must be those of the pairing that failed the assertion, on
one object. The file keeps its benchmark name: the model the solver finds,
and with it the free symbols, changes with it.
